	/**
	 * Companion System (2026-07-19, per user request: "if a companion
	 * dies, the next time the user spawns it in, it comes back alive
	 * again") -- overrides AiAgent's own notifyObjectDestructionObservers(),
	 * the real entrypoint every creature's death funnels through the
	 * moment a HAM pool hits zero (CreatureObjectImplementation::
	 * inflictDamage() -> here). The stock version routes non-pet AiAgents
	 * into CreatureManager::notifyDestruction() -- the full corpse/loot/XP/
	 * faction NPC-death pipeline, none of which makes sense for a player's
	 * own companion. This override skips all of that entirely: the
	 * companion is immediately stored and marked dead-until-resummoned on
	 * its control device (CompanionControlDevice::handleCompanionDeath()),
	 * which CompanionControlDeviceImplementation::spawnObject() now
	 * auto-clears on the next summon attempt instead of blocking it -- see
	 * NOTES.md.
	 * @pre { this, attacker locked }
	 * @post { this, attacker locked }
	 */
	@preLocked
	@arg1preLocked
	public native int notifyObjectDestructionObservers(TangibleObject attacker, int condition, boolean isCombatAction);

